Each `document.querySelector` or `document.querySelectorAll` is a relatively timeconsuming
operation..
```js
const parent = document.querySelector("#parent");

for (let i of data) {
	...
	parent.appendChild()
}
// Or
for (let i of data) {
	...
	document.QuerySelector("#parent").appendChild(...)
}
//The first one has better performance.
```
